  <Table name="GIDesign">
    <Row>
      <DesignID>87cbc430-9031-4a59-9801-e1e060df2f41</DesignID>
      <AiDescription>Field references in text are:
BOM number = BOM ID
BOM revision = revision
Inventory part number = inventory id
Item description = item descr
BOM description = BOM descr
Item class = Class ID
Item class type = type
BOM status = status
BOM start date = start date
BOM end date = end date
Warehouse default BOM = whse default bom
Warehouse lot size = whse lot size

This dataset shows summary information for bills of materials, or BOMs. &amp;nbsp;Row data includes BOM number, bom revision, inventory part number, item description, bom description, item class, item class type, warehouse id, BOM status, BOM start date, BOM end date, Warehouse default, and Warehouse lot size.

There is no detail information for inventory parts in this data set. &amp;nbsp;

An inventory part may have multiple BOMs to make the item. &amp;nbsp;The item class type indicates if the BOM produces a subassembly used in another BOM, or if it produces a finished good. &amp;nbsp;The bom status indicates if the bom revision is currently used in the system. &amp;nbsp;The start and end dates indicate the range of time that a bom revision is valid. &amp;nbsp;If there is no end date, and the bom status is active, the bom revision is still valid. &amp;nbsp;The warehouse default bom indicates the bom revision to use for the production of the item within that warehouse.</AiDescription>
